WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
How can a dent in clay show what lived somewhere millions of years ago?

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.500
In about thirty minutes at your table, you and your child make fossil prints.

3
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.780
Together, you turn those prints into clues.

4
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.340
This activity gives your child hands-on practice looking closely at small details.

5
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.220
They match ridges, leaf veins, and footprints to real objects.

6
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.820
They also practice making a guess and checking it against clues.

7
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.120
Older kids can practice patience waiting for a cast.

8
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:36.123
Stay with your child the whole time.

9
00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:40.183
Keep all small objects away from children under four.

10
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:42.883
Cover the table with newspaper.

11
00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:46.643
Use store-bought modeling clay that stays soft.

12
00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:49.323
Skip homemade flour dough.

13
00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:55.183
Gather empty, clean shells with smooth edges, a pinecone, and toy animals.

14
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:57.683
Discard cracked shells.

15
00:00:58.863 --> 00:01:02.103
Choose leaves from plants you know and avoid poison ivy.

16
00:01:02.903 --> 00:01:04.803
Never taste plants or clay.

17
00:01:05.867 --> 00:01:10.047
Have your child knead an orange-sized ball of clay until it softens.

18
00:01:11.347 --> 00:01:13.747
Use a rolling pin or smooth plastic jar.

19
00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:19.067
Flatten the clay on a paper plate until it is about two centimeters thick.

20
00:01:20.387 --> 00:01:23.027
Press the shell straight down, then lift it straight up.

21
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.567
That hollow print is a mold.

22
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.330
Make some prints while your child looks away.

23
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.630
Swap plates and ask, “What made this print?”

24
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.970
Then ask, “What clue helped you guess?”

25
00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.990
Match the prints to the objects.

26
00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.130
A ridged scallop shell points to the sea.

27
00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.050
A leaf points to land with plants.

28
00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.653
Try a quick prediction before your next print.

29
00:01:47.913 --> 00:01:50.293
Use a ridged shell and a leaf with thick veins.

30
00:01:51.713 --> 00:01:55.673
Which details do you think will still show up after you lift the objects away?

31
00:02:01.233 --> 00:02:03.073
Press and lift each object.

32
00:02:04.393 --> 00:02:07.713
Compare the shell ridges and leaf veins with their hollow prints.

33
00:02:09.013 --> 00:02:14.013
In Virginia, fossil scallops in river cliffs show that a shallow sea once covered

34
00:02:14.013 --> 00:02:17.173
that land. The scallops lived in the sea.

35
00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:22.197
If you choose to make a cast, only an adult handles the plaster.

36
00:02:23.477 --> 00:02:25.817
Work outdoors or by a wide-open window.

37
00:02:27.137 --> 00:02:28.597
Keep children and pets away.

38
00:02:29.897 --> 00:02:33.517
Wear a NIOSH-approved dust mask, eye protection, and gloves.

39
00:02:34.877 --> 00:02:36.677
Never put any body part in plaster.

40
00:02:38.077 --> 00:02:39.077
It can get hot.

41
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.670
Build a clay wall about two centimeters high.

42
00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:47.090
Mix the plaster as directed and pour it into the mold.

43
00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.390
Keep children back until it cools.

44
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.890
It hardens in about thirty to sixty minutes.

45
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:56.350
Leave it overnight to dry.

46
00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.790
Then peel off the clay to see the raised cast.

47
00:03:00.883 --> 00:03:05.743
For ages five to seven, skip the plaster and sort prints into water and land.

48
00:03:07.043 --> 00:03:09.263
For ages eight to ten, try a sand dig.

49
00:03:10.563 --> 00:03:13.003
Use lightly damp play sand below face height.

50
00:03:14.523 --> 00:03:16.783
Bury shells, leaf prints, or hardened casts.

51
00:03:18.143 --> 00:03:20.383
Brush gently and keep the sand in the tub.

52
00:03:21.763 --> 00:03:23.883
Wash hands with soap and water when you finish.

53
00:03:25.223 --> 00:03:29.043
Your child used shapes as clues, just as scientists do with fossils.
